<title>JAPAN: Japan companies agree on DVD-RAM standard - paper.</title>
<headline>Japan companies agree on DVD-RAM standard - paper.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Major electric appliance makers, including Matsushita Electric Industrial Co Ltd, Toshiba Corp and Sony Corp, have agreed to unify standards used on digital video disc random access memories (DVD-RAMs), a Japanese business daily reported on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The Nihon Keizai Shimbun said that the unified DVD-RAM standard is expected to be introduced in April.</p>
<p>DVD-RAM, a new memory medium for computers the size of a compact disc, can store image data worth about one hour.</p>
</text>
